## Choice B: General JSON serialization with `recipients`
If your JWE has:
```json
{
  "protected": "...",
  "recipients": [
    { "header": { "kid": "a" }, "encrypted_key": "..." },
    { "header": { "kid": "b" }, "encrypted_key": "..." }
  ],
  "iv": "...",
  "ciphertext": "...",
  "tag": "..."
}
```

Then you must:

1. Pick the correct recipient, usually by matching `kid`
2. Build compact serialization from:
   - `protected`
   - selected recipient's `encrypted_key`
   - `iv`
   - `ciphertext`
   - `tag`

### Example
```csharp
using System.Text.Json;
using Jose;

string targetKid = "my-key";
var doc = JsonDocument.Parse(File.ReadAllText("jwe.json"));
var root = doc.RootElement;

string protectedHeader = root.GetProperty("protected").GetString;
string iv = root.GetProperty("iv").GetString;
string ciphertext = root.GetProperty("ciphertext").GetString;
string tag = root.GetProperty("tag").GetString;

string encryptedKey = null;

foreach (var recipient in root.GetProperty("recipients").EnumerateArray)
{
    if (recipient.TryGetProperty("header", out var header) &&
        header.TryGetProperty("kid", out var kidProp) &&
        kidProp.GetString == targetKid)
    {
        encryptedKey = recipient.GetProperty("encrypted_key").GetString;
        break;
    }
}

if (encryptedKey == null)
    throw new Exception("Matching recipient not found.");

string compact = $"{protectedHeader}.{encryptedKey}.{iv}.{ciphertext}.{tag}";
string payload = JWT.Decode(compact, rsa);

Console.WriteLine(payload);
```

